fix(servers): editing a saved server stops silently minting a second one, and its password field starts working

Two ways the edit sheet lied about what Save does.

**Identity.** Only the protocol toggle was locked, so Address and Username stayed typeable. Rust mints the volume id
from `(host, port, username)` and `sftp_known_servers::remember` keys on the same tuple, so `update_saved_server` on an
edited one UPSERTS a new pinned entry beside the old: the hub and the switcher both grow a duplicate row, the old row
still points at the previous account, and any tab on the old volume id is orphaned. Nothing said so on screen. All three
identity fields are locked now, with `servers.sheet.identityLocked` under them naming the path that actually works
(Forget, then Add). The "paste whatever you have" address help steps aside when nobody can type in the field.

**Password.** `ServerFormFields` binds `form.secret` in edit mode too, but `save()` only sent `serverTargetFrom(form)`,
which carries no secret. Typing a new password and pressing Save did nothing at all, with no feedback. It now writes
through `saveSftpCredentials` / `saveWebdavCredentials` on the target's tuple and the Remember box reports on, because
the store holds one. An empty field still means "I didn't come here to change the password", never "store an empty one".
The write lands after the Remember flip, so a password typed in the same visit wins over a box turned off: a field with
text in it and Save pressed stores that password.

- `identityEditable` + `identityHint` on `ServerFormFields`, off in edit mode.
- `writeTypedSecret` in `SignInSheet.svelte`, keyed on the `ServerTarget`'s own tuple.
- Three cells: the locked fields plus the visible hint, a typed password reaching the Keychain with the right tuple, and
  an empty one leaving the store alone.
- `servers.sheet.identityLocked` translated into all ten locales, terms sourced from each catalog's existing
  `menu.network.forgetServer` and `servers.hub.addServer` so the hint matches the buttons it points at.
